The method processes the result set using the callback function provided by the user. If there are any errors during this process, an exception is thrown with a message explaining the problem.

Finally, the method returns the `IDataReader` object or an appropriate error message based on the success of the operation. The method also includes concurrency and scalability features to handle high-throughput requests efficiently and optimize performance under stress conditions.']

