ws = websocket.WebSocket()
ws.connect("ws://localhost:8080")

# Send data to the server
ws.send("123\n456\n789\n")

# Close the connection
ws.close()
```
This will send three lines of integers to the WebSocket server, and the program should print out the maximum value encountered so far after each line is processed. You can adjust the number of threads used for processing data from WebSocket connections by modifying the `num_threads` variable in the `main()` function.']

