Here is an example of how you could implement the described IoT sensor data aggregation and analytics platform in Java:
```
public class SensorDataAggregator {
    private static final int MAX_CONCURRENT_REQUESTS = 100; // Maximum number of concurrent requests to process
    private static final int MAX_EVENTS_PER_SECOND = 150000; // Maximum number of events per second to process
    private static final int MAX_DEVICE_TYPES = 500; // Maximum number of device types to support

    private Map<String, SensorData> sensorDataMap; // Map of sensor data by device ID
    private List<SensorDataProcessor> sensorDataProcessors; // List of sensor data processors to handle events
    private MessageQueue messageQueue; // Queue for incoming messages
    private DocumentStore documentStore; // Document store for storing historical sensor data
    private TimeSeriesDatabase timeSeriesDatabase; // Time-series database for storing recent sensor data

    public SensorDataAggregator() {
        this.sensorDataMap = new ConcurrentHashMap<>();
        this.sensorDataProcessors = new ArrayList<>();
        this.messageQueue = new MessageQueue();
        this.documentStore = new DocumentStore(this);
        this.timeSeriesDatabase = new TimeSeriesDatabase(this);
    }

    public void start() {
        // Start message queue and document store
        this.messageQueue.start();
        this.documentStore.start();

        // Start sensor data processors
        for (SensorDataProcessor processor : this.sensorDataProcessors) {
            processor.start();
        }
    }

    public void stop() {
        // Stop message queue and document store
        this.messageQueue.stop();
        this.documentStore.stop();

        // Stop sensor data processors
        for (SensorDataProcessor processor : this.sensorDataProcessors) {
            processor.stop();
        }
    }

    public void handleMessage(String message) throws IOException, InterruptedException {
        // Parse incoming message
        IncomingMessage incomingMessage = parseIncomingMessage(message);

        // Update sensor data map
        String deviceId = incomingMessage.getDeviceId();
        SensorData sensorData = this.sensorDataMap.get(deviceId);
        if (sensorData == null) {
            sensorData = new SensorData(deviceId, incomingMessage.getTimestamp());
            this.sensorDataMap.put(deviceId, sensorData);
        }
        sensorData.updateWithIncomingMessage(incomingMessage);

        // Handle incoming message in all processors
        for (SensorDataProcessor processor : this.sensorDataProcessors) {
            processor.handleIncomingMessage(incomingMessage);
        }
    }

    public void handleDeviceDisconnect(String deviceId) throws IOException, InterruptedException {
        // Remove sensor data from map
        SensorData sensorData = this.sensorDataMap.remove(deviceId);

        // Handle disconnection in all processors
        for (SensorDataProcessor processor : this.sensorDataProcessors) {
            processor.handleDeviceDisconnect(deviceId, sensorData);
        }
    }

    public void handleDeviceReconnect(String deviceId) throws IOException, InterruptedException {
        // Handle reconnect in all processors
        for (SensorDataProcessor processor : this.sensorDataProcessors) {
            processor.handleDeviceReconnect(deviceId);
        }
    }

    public void handleMessageQueueError(String error) throws IOException, InterruptedException {
        // Handle message queue error in all processors
        for (SensorDataProcessor processor : this.sensorDataProcessors) {
            processor.handleMessageQueueError(error);
        }
    }

    public void handleDocumentStoreError(String error) throws IOException, InterruptedException {
        // Handle document store error in all processors
        for (SensorDataProcessor processor : this.sensorDataProcessors) {
            processor.handleDocumentStoreError(error);
        }
    }

    public void handleTimeSeriesDatabaseError(String error) throws IOException, InterruptedException {
        // Handle time-series database error in all processors
        for (SensorDataProcessor processor : this.sensorDataProcessors) {
            processor.handleTimeSeriesDatabaseError(error);
        }
    }

    private IncomingMessage parseIncomingMessage(String message) throws IOException, InterruptedException {
        // Parse incoming message and extract device ID and timestamp
        String[] tokens = message.split("\\s+");
        String deviceId = tokens[0];
        long timestamp = Long.parseLong(tokens[1]);

        // Create new incoming message with device ID and timestamp
        IncomingMessage incomingMessage = new IncomingMessage(deviceId, timestamp);

        // Update sensor data map with new incoming message
        this.sensorDataMap.put(deviceId, incomingMessage);

        return incomingMessage;
    }
}

public class SensorDataProcessor {
    private static final int MAX_CONCURRENT_REQUESTS = 100; // Maximum number of concurrent requests to process
    private static final int MAX_EVENTS_PER_SECOND = 150000; // Maximum number of events per second to process

    private SensorDataAggregator sensorDataAggregator; // Reference to the sensor data aggregator
    private List<String> deviceIds; // List of device IDs to process
    private Map<String, Double> latestSensorReadings; // Map of latest sensor readings by device ID

    public SensorDataProcessor(SensorDataAggregator sensorDataAggregator) {
        this.sensorDataAggregator = sensorDataAggregator;
        this.deviceIds = new ArrayList<>();
        this.latestSensorReadings = new HashMap<>();
    }

    public void start() throws IOException, InterruptedException {
        // Start message queue and document store
        this.sensorDataAggregator.start();

        // Start sensor data processors
        for (String deviceId : this.deviceIds) {
            this.latestSensorReadings.put(deviceId, 0.0);
        }
    }

    public void stop() throws IOException, InterruptedException {
        // Stop message queue and document store
        this.sensorDataAggregator.stop();

        // Stop sensor data processors
        for (String deviceId : this.deviceIds) {
            this.latestSensorReadings.remove(deviceId);
        }
    }

    public void handleIncomingMessage(IncomingMessage incomingMessage) throws IOException, InterruptedException {
        // Handle incoming message in all processors
        for (String deviceId : this.deviceIds) {
            if (incomingMessage.getDeviceId().equals(deviceId)) {
                double sensorReading = incomingMessage.getSensorReading();
                this.latestSensorReadings.put(deviceId, sensorReading);
            }
        }
    }

    public void handleDeviceDisconnect(String deviceId) throws IOException, InterruptedException {
        // Handle disconnection in all processors
        for (String deviceId : this.deviceIds) {
            if (incomingMessage.getDeviceId().equals(deviceId)) {
                this.latestSensorReadings.remove(deviceId);
            }
        }
    }

    public void handleDeviceReconnect(String deviceId) throws IOException, InterruptedException {
        // Handle reconnect in all processors
        for (String deviceId : this.deviceIds) {
            if (incomingMessage.getDeviceId().equals(deviceId)) {
                this.latestSensorReadings.put(deviceId, 0.0);
            }
        }
    }

    public void handleMessageQueueError(String error) throws IOException, InterruptedException {
        // Handle message queue error in all processors
        for (String deviceId : this.deviceIds) {
            if (incomingMessage.getDeviceId().equals(deviceId)) {
                this.latestSensorReadings.remove(deviceId);
            }
        }
    }

    public void handleDocumentStoreError(String error) throws IOException, InterruptedException {
        // Handle document store error in all processors
        for (String deviceId : this.deviceIds) {
            if (incomingMessage.getDeviceId().equals(deviceId)) {
                this.latestSensorReadings.remove(deviceId);
            }
        }
    }

    public void handleTimeSeriesDatabaseError(String error) throws IOException, InterruptedException {
        // Handle time-series database error in all processors
        for (String deviceId : this.deviceIds) {
            if (incomingMessage.getDeviceId().equals(deviceId)) {
                this.latestSensorReadings.remove(deviceId);
            }
        }
    }

    public double getLatestSensorReading(String deviceId) throws IOException, InterruptedException {
        return this.latestSensorReadings.getOrDefault(deviceId, 0.0);
    }
}
```

In this example, we have two classes: `SensorDataAggregator` and `SensorDataProcessor`. The `SensorDataAggregator` class is responsible for handling incoming messages from the message queue, updating a map of latest sensor readings by device ID, and handling disconnections and reconnects. The `SensorDataProcessor` class is responsible for processing incoming messages and retrieving the latest sensor reading for each device ID.

The `SensorDataAggregator` class has the following methods:

* `start()`: Starts the message queue and document store, and starts all sensor data processors.
* `stop()`: Stops the message queue and document store, and stops all sensor data processors.
* `handleMessage(String message)`: Handles an incoming message from the message queue by updating the map of latest sensor readings for each device ID.
* `handleDeviceDisconnect(String deviceId)`: Handles a disconnection event for a specific device ID by removing it from the map of latest sensor readings.
* `handleDeviceReconnect(String deviceId)`: Handles a reconnect event for a specific device ID by adding it back to the map of latest sensor readings with an initial reading value of 0.0.
* `handleMessageQueueError(String error)`: Handles any errors that occur in the message queue by removing the corresponding device IDs from the map of latest sensor readings.
* `handleDocumentStoreError(String error)`: Handles any errors that occur in the document store by removing the corresponding device IDs from the map of latest sensor readings.
* `getLatestSensorReading(String deviceId)`: Returns the latest sensor reading for a specific device ID, or 0.0 if no reading is available.

The `SensorDataProcessor` class has the following methods:

* `start()`: Starts the message queue and document store, and starts all sensor data processors.
* `stop()`: Stops the message queue and document store, and stops all sensor data processors.
* `handleIncomingMessage(IncomingMessage incomingMessage)`: Handles an incoming message by updating the map of latest sensor readings for each device ID.
* `handleDeviceDisconnect(String deviceId)`: Handles a disconnection event for a specific device ID by removing it from the map of latest sensor readings.
* `handleDeviceReconnect(String deviceId)`: Handles a reconnect event for a specific device ID by adding it back to the map of latest sensor readings with an initial reading value of 0.0.
* `handleMessageQueueError(String error)`: Handles any errors that occur in the message queue by removing the corresponding device IDs from the map of latest sensor readings.
* `handleDocumentStoreError(String error)`: Handles any errors that occur in the document store by removing the corresponding device IDs from the map of latest sensor readings.
* `getLatestSensorReading(String deviceId)`: Returns the latest sensor reading for a specific device ID, or 0.0 if no reading is available.

In this example, we have used the `Map` data structure to store the latest sensor readings by device ID. The map allows us to quickly retrieve the latest reading for each device ID, and also provides a way to handle disconnections and reconnects by removing the corresponding device IDs from the map.

Note that this is just one possible implementation of a sensor data aggregator and processor using Java. There are many other ways to implement these components, and the specific implementation will depend on the requirements of your system.']

