## Advantages and Disadvantages

The advantages of using a modular approach in video processing are:

* Modular code is easier to maintain and update than monolithic code.
* Modular code is more scalable and can be easily reused in different projects.
* Modular code is more organized and can be easily understood by other developers.
* Modular code is more flexible and can be used for different types of videos.
* Modular code can be tested separately, which makes it easier to identify the source of errors.

The disadvantages of using a modular approach in video processing are:

* Modular code can be harder to understand than monolithic code.
* Modular code can be harder to debug and optimize.
* Modular code requires more effort to set up and configure.
* Modular code may not perform as well as monolithic code in certain situations.

## Conclusion

In this project, we have designed a modular video processing system that uses separate modules for different video processing tasks such as initialization, processing, encoding, and playback. The system is designed to be modular, scalable, and flexible, which makes it easy to maintain and update. We have also discussed the advantages and disadvantages of using a modular approach in video processing.']

