Here is a proposed implementation of the highly scalable, modular, and configurable logging framework in C:

1. Logging Service Interface
---------------------------

The logging service interface defines the methods that will be used to interact with the external logging services. It includes functions for configuring log levels, formats, and priorities, as well as sending logs to the external services.
```c
typedef struct {
    void (*set_log_level)(int level);
    void (*set_log_format)(const char *format);
    void (*set_log_priority)(int priority);
    void (*send_log)(const char *message);
} logging_service;
```
2. Logging Service Plugin Architecture
--------------------------------------

The plugin architecture enables the integration with multiple external logging services. It includes a registry of available logging services and a mechanism for dynamically loading and unloading plugins.
```c
typedef struct {
    const char *name;
    logging_service service;
} logging_plugin;

void register_logging_plugin(const char *name, logging_service service);
void unregister_logging_plugin(const char *name);
```
3. Logging Framework
-------------------

The logging framework includes the functionality for managing log levels, formats, and priorities, as well as sending logs to external services. It also includes real-time monitoring capabilities through a web-based dashboard.
```c
typedef struct {
    void (*set_log_level)(int level);
    void (*set_log_format)(const char *format);
    void (*set_log_priority)(int priority);
    void (*send_log)(const char *message);
    void (*monitor_logs)();
} logging_framework;
```
4. Logging Configuration
-------------------------

The logging configuration includes the current log levels, formats, and priorities for each module in the system. It also includes a mechanism for updating configurations without causing downtime.
```c
typedef struct {
    int level;
    const char *format;
    int priority;
} logging_configuration;

void update_logging_configuration(const logging_configuration *config);
```
5. Logging Buffer
-----------------

The logging buffer is a local buffer that stores logs before they are sent to the external services. It includes a mechanism for dynamically tuning the buffer size based on system load and external service availability.
```c
typedef struct {
    char *buffer;
    int capacity;
    int size;
} logging_buffer;

void initialize_logging_buffer(int capacity);
