```
6. Logging Module
------------------

Each module in the system has its own logging instance, which is responsible for sending logs to the external services and managing the log levels, formats, and priorities. The logging module also includes a mechanism for updating configurations without causing downtime.
```c
typedef struct {
    const char *name;
    int level;
    const char *format;
    int priority;
    logging_service service;
} logging_module;

void initialize_logging_module(const char *name, const logging_configuration *config);
void update_logging_module(const char *name, const logging_configuration *config);
```
7. Real-Time Monitoring Dashboard
---------------------------------

The real-time monitoring dashboard allows administrators to view and adjust logging verbosity and configuration settings through a web-based interface. It includes mechanisms for updating configurations without causing downtime and ensuring the system handles large-scale distributed applications where individual components may have different logging policies and requirements.
```c
typedef struct {
    void (*start_dashboard)();
    void (*stop_dashboard)();
} logging_dashboard;
```
8. Diagnostic Tool
------------------

The diagnostic tool is used to monitor and resolve logging failures, including retry logic and fallback strategies for failed external service communications. It also includes mechanisms for updating configurations without causing downtime.
```c
typedef struct {
    void (*start_diagnostics)();
    void (*stop_diagnostics)();
} logging_diagnostic;
```
9. Fault Tolerance and Adaptability
-----------------------------------

The framework is designed to be resilient to network partitions, service outages, and varying loads. It includes mechanisms for fault tolerance and adaptability in real-world conditions.
```c
typedef struct {
    void (*start_fault_tolerance)();
    void (*stop_fault_tolerance)();
} logging_fault_tolerance;
```
10. Unit Testing
-----------------

The code is thoroughly tested to ensure that it meets the requirements and is maintainable. It includes comprehensive unit tests covering edge cases and performance bottlenecks.
```c
