The `processReading()` function takes a new `SensorReading` object as input and adds it to the appropriate `Sensor` object in the `SensorReader`. The `getMostRecentReadings()` function returns a vector of `SensorReading` objects, each representing the most recent sensor reading for a specific sensor.

In the `main()` function, we initialize an instance of the `SensorReader` class with the names of three sensors. We then process a new sensor reading using the `processReading()` function and get the most recent sensor readings using the `getMostRecentReadings()` function. Finally, we print the most recent sensor readings to the console.

Note that this is just a sample code and may need to be modified to fit your specific use case. Additionally, you will need to ensure that the code is scalable and efficient for handling large datasets of sensor readings.']

