The `TelemetryProcessor` class is responsible for processing telemetry messages from IoT devices. It has the following methods:

* `ProcessMessageAsync`: This method processes a single message from an IoT device and passes it to the appropriate data processor (either a remote or local one) to handle it. If no data processor exists for the device, it creates a new one using the provided parameters.
* `ProcessMessageBatchAsync`: This method processes a batch of messages from multiple IoT devices at once. It calls the `ProcessMessageAsync` method for each message in the batch.
* `InitializeAsync`: This method initializes the telemetry processor by creating data processors for all of the IoT devices that are registered with it.
* `ShutdownAsync`: This method shuts down the telemetry processor by shutting down all of the data processors that it created.

The `DeviceTelemetryDataProcessor` class is responsible for processing telemetry messages from a single IoT device. It has the following methods:

* `ProcessMessageAsync`: This method processes a single message from an IoT device and passes it to the appropriate data processor (either a remote or local one) to handle it. If no data processor exists for the device, it creates a new one using the provided parameters.
* `InitializeAsync`: This method initializes the data processor by connecting to the IoT hub and subscribing to telemetry messages from the specified device.
* `ShutdownAsync`: This method shuts down the data processor by unsubscribing from telemetry messages from the specified device and disconnecting from the IoT hub.']

