    int sampling_interval;
    std::string data_format; // CSV, JSON, etc.
    std::string protocol; // HTTP, MQTT, etc.
    bool enable_encryption;
    // ...
};
```

3. **Real-Time and Historical Data Storage and Query Optimization**:

The library uses a caching layer to improve query performance for frequently accessed data, reducing load on the underlying storage system. This caching layer is implemented using a combination of in-memory and disk-based storage. The in-memory cache stores frequently accessed data in RAM, while the disk-based storage stores less frequently accessed data.

The library also optimizes data indexing and partitioning strategies to handle large datasets efficiently. This involves using techniques such as database sharding, which distributes the data across multiple nodes based on certain criteria (e.g., sensor ID, time stamp).

To ensure data integrity and minimize contention during queries, the library uses a distributed lock mechanism that ensures only one thread can access a particular node at any given time.

```c++
// In-memory cache for frequently accessed data
struct Cache {
    std::map<int, SensorData> data; // sensor ID -> data mapping
};

// Disk-based storage for less frequently accessed data
struct Storage {
    std::vector<SensorData> data;
};

// Query function
std::vector<SensorData> query(const std::string &sensor_id, const std::string &time_range) {
    // Acquire a lock on the node that contains the requested data
    std::unique_lock<std::mutex> lock(getNodeLock(sensor_id));

    // Retrieve the data from the cache or storage
    Cache cache = getCache();
    Storage storage = getStorage();

    // Filter the data based on the time range
    std::vector<SensorData> filtered_data;
    for (auto &data : cache.data) {
        if (data.first == sensor_id && isInTimeRange(data.second, time_range)) {
            filtered_data.push_back(data.second);
        }
    }

    // Combine the filtered data with the data from storage
    for (auto &data : storage.data) {
        if (data.first == sensor_id && isInTimeRange(data.second, time_range)) {
            filtered_data.push_back(data.second);
        }
    }

    // Release the lock and return the filtered data
    releaseNodeLock(sensor_id);
    return filtered_data;
}
```

4. **Security**:

The library uses secure communication protocols such as HTTPS to protect data in transit, and encryption techniques such as AES-256 to ensure the confidentiality of stored data. Additionally, it uses secure authentication mechanisms such as OAuth 2.0 to authenticate clients and authorize their access to sensitive data.

