#### 2.5.6 `NFAPI_SYS_INFO_INDICATION` message

The `NFAPI_SYS_INFO_INDICATION` message is sent by the PNF to the NF in response to an `NFAPI_SYS_INFO_REQUEST` message, and contains system information related to the cell. The `NFAPI_SYS_INFO_INDICATION` message contains a list of `NFAPI_SYS_INFO_BLOCK` structures, each of which contains system information for a particular subcarrier group within the cell.

The `NFAPI_SYS_INFO_BLOCK` structure is defined as follows:
```c
typedef struct {
    uint16_t             sfn;
    uint8_t              slot;
    uint8_t              subcarrier_spacing;
    uint8_t              cyclic_prefix;
    uint8_t              number_of_subcarriers;
    uint8_t              scs;
    uint8_t              transmission_mode;
    int16_t             *tx_data;
} NFAPI_SYS_INFO_BLOCK;
```
The `sfn` field specifies the subframe number within a frame. The `slot` field specifies the slot within a subframe. The `subcarrier_spacing` field specifies the subcarrier spacing for this block, and must be set to one of the following values:
* 15 (kHz)
* 30 (kHz)
* 60 (kHz)
* 120 (kHz)
* 240 (kHz)

The `cyclic_prefix` field specifies the cyclic prefix for this block, and must be set to one of the following values:
* NFAPI_CP_NORMAL
* NFAPI_CP_EXTENDED

The `number_of_subcarriers` field specifies the number of subcarriers in this block. The `scs` field specifies the scs for this block, and must be set to one of the following values:
* 0 (15kHz)
* 1 (30kHz)
* 2 (60kHz)
* 3 (120kHz)
* 4 (240kHz)

The `transmission_mode` field specifies the transmission mode for this block, and must be set to one of the following values:
* NFAPI_TM_1
* NFAPI_TM_2
* NFAPI_TM_3

The `tx_data` field contains a list of 16-bit signed integers that represent the transmitted data. The number of elements in this list is equal to the value of the `number_of_subcarriers` field, and each element represents one subcarrier group within the block.

The following code snippet demonstrates how to send a `NFAPI_SYS_INFO_INDICATION` message:
```c
#include <nfapi/oai_integration/nfapi_nr_pnf.h>

// Set up NFAPI structure
nfapi_nr_pnf_t nfapi;
nfapi_initialize(&nfapi);

// Configure NFAPI structure for PNF
nfapi.pnf = 1;
nfapi.pnf_nr = 1;

// Set up system information block list
NFAPI_SYS_INFO_BLOCK sys_info_block;
sys_info_block.sfn = 10;
sys_info_block.slot = 3;
sys_info_block.subcarrier_spacing = NFAPI_SCS_60KHZ;
sys_info_block.cyclic_prefix = NFAPI_CP_NORMAL;
sys_info_block.number_of_subcarriers = 10;
sys_info_block.scs = 3;
sys_info_block.transmission_mode = NFAPI_TM_2;
sys_info_block.tx_data = calloc(10, sizeof(int16_t));
for (int i = 0; i < 10; i++) {
    sys_info_block.tx_data[i] = rand() % 100 - 50;
}

// Set up system information list
NFAPI_SYS_INFO_LIST sys_info_list;
sys_info_list.number_of_blocks = 1;
sys_info_list.block = &sys_info_block;

// Send system information indication message
nfapi_nr_pnf_system_information_ind(&nfapi, &sys_info_list);

// Clean up
free(sys_info_block.tx_data);
```
