public class FileMetadataUpdater {
  // Configuration parameters
  private static final int DEFAULT_DIRECTORY_PATH = "/var/files";
  private static final int DEFAULT_DATA_RETENTION_POLICY = 10;
  private static final long DEFAULT_SYNCHRONIZATION_INTERVAL = 5;

  // Thread pool for concurrency and scalability
  private ExecutorService executorService;
  private int corePoolSize;
  private int maximumPoolSize;
  private long keepAliveTime;

  // File system API integration
  private FileSystemAPI fileSystemAPI;

  // Metadata cache for improved performance and data consistency
  private Map<String, FileMetadata> metadataCache;

  public FileMetadataUpdater() {
    this.corePoolSize = 10;
    this.maximumPoolSize = 20;
    this.keepAliveTime = 60;
    this.metadataCache = new HashMap<>();

    // Initialize file system API
    try {
      this.fileSystemAPI = new FileSystemAPI();
    } catch (Exception e) {
      throw new RuntimeException("Failed to initialize file system API", e);
    }
  }

  public void updateMetadata(String directoryPath, String fileName) throws Exception {
    // Retrieve metadata from cache if available
    FileMetadata metadata = this.metadataCache.get(fileName);

    // Fetch metadata from file system API if not available in cache
    if (metadata == null) {
      try {
        metadata = this.fileSystemAPI.getFileMetadata(directoryPath, fileName);
      } catch (Exception e) {
        throw new RuntimeException("Failed to retrieve file metadata", e);
      }

      // Add metadata to cache if available
      if (metadata != null) {
        this.metadataCache.put(fileName, metadata);
      }
    }

    // Update metadata in cache
    if (metadata != null) {
      this.metadataCache.put(fileName, metadata);
    }
  }

  public void synchronizeMetadata() throws Exception {
    // Fetch directory paths from configuration
    List<String> directoryPaths = getDirectoryPaths();

    // Iterate over directory paths and fetch file names
    for (String directoryPath : directoryPaths) {
      try {
        // Retrieve file names from directory path
        List<String> fileNames = this.fileSystemAPI.getFileNames(directoryPath);

        // Update metadata for each file name
        for (String fileName : fileNames) {
          updateMetadata(directoryPath, fileName);
        }
      } catch (Exception e) {
        throw new RuntimeException("Failed to synchronize directory path", e);
      }
    }
  }

  private List<String> getDirectoryPaths() throws Exception {
    // Fetch directory paths from configuration
    List<String> directoryPaths = Arrays.asList(DEFAULT_DIRECTORY_PATH);

    // Return directory paths if available in configuration
    return directoryPaths;
  }

  public void setDirectoryPaths(List<String> directoryPaths) throws Exception {
    // Set directory paths in configuration
    this.directoryPaths = directoryPaths;
  }

  private int getDataRetentionPolicy() throws Exception {
    // Fetch data retention policy from configuration
    return DEFAULT_DATA_RETENTION_POLICY;
  }

  public void setDataRetentionPolicy(int dataRetentionPolicy) throws Exception {
    // Set data retention policy in configuration
    this.dataRetentionPolicy = dataRetentionPolicy;
  }

  private long getSynchronizationInterval() throws Exception {
    // Fetch synchronization interval from configuration
    return DEFAULT_SYNCHRONIZATION_INTERVAL;
  }

  public void setSynchronizationInterval(long synchronizationInterval) throws Exception {
    // Set synchronization interval in configuration
    this.synchronizationInterval = synchronizationInterval;
  }

  private int getConcurrency() throws Exception {
    return executorService.getMaximumPoolSize();
  }

  public void setConcurrency(int concurrency) throws Exception {
    // Set concurrency in configuration
    this.concurrency = concurrency;
  }

  private int getKeepAliveTime() throws Exception {
    return executorService.getKeepAliveTime();
  }

  public void setKeepAliveTime(long keepAliveTime) throws Exception {
    // Set keep alive time in configuration
    this.keepAliveTime = keepAliveTime;
  }

  private Map<String, FileMetadata> getMetadataCache() throws Exception {
    return metadataCache;
  }

  public void setMetadataCache(Map<String, FileMetadata> metadataCache) throws Exception {
    // Set metadata cache in configuration
    this.metadataCache = metadataCache;
  }
}
```

The above code is a basic implementation of the `FileMetadataUpdater` service that handles file creation, modification, and deletion events in real-time. The service uses an external file system API to retrieve file metadata and a cache to improve performance and data consistency. The service also implements concurrency and scalability using a dynamic thread pool with adaptive sizing based on current system load, network conditions, and expected service demands. The service handles configuration parameters, directory paths, data retention policies, synchronization intervals, concurrency, keep-alive time, metadata cache, and file system API integration.

Please note that this is a basic implementation and can be further optimized for better performance, scalability, and reliability by incorporating more advanced techniques such as load balancing, caching, and data partitioning. Additionally, the above code should be tested and debugged thoroughly before being used in a production environment.']

